  "title": "FDA Recalls Nearly 300,000 Blood Thinner Capsules Over Quality Concerns: What Patients Need to Know",
  "summary": "The U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has announced the voluntary recall of nearly 300,000 blood thinner capsules due to concerns related to product quality and impurity levels. The recalled medication contains dabigatran etexilate, a commonly prescribed anticoagulant sold under the brand name Pradaxa. The recall affects specific lots manufactured by Alkem Laboratories Ltd., based in Mumbai, India, and distributed across the United States by Major Pharmaceuticals of Indianapolis. Accordin",
